# C3DW WORKSHOP — CLINE OPERATING RULES
Last revised: 2026-09-23, after a full architecture audit. Full rationale for every rule below lives in `website-architecture-audit.md` in the Claude project — this file is the checklist, not the explanation. Keep it that way: if a rule needs a paragraph to justify, the justification belongs in the audit doc, not here.

## CURRENT ARCHITECTURE — READ FIRST
- Live site: `web/`. Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind 4, Supabase via `@supabase/ssr`. Vercel builds and deploys it (Root Directory = `web`) on every push to `main`.
- `main` is the only active branch. `feature/universal-web-target` is abandoned — it stopped before the Next.js scaffold existed. Do not branch from it or treat it as current.
- Everything at the repo root (`index.html`, `hub.html`, `gallery.html`, `contact.html`, `meettheteam.html`, `request.html`, `inventory.html`, `main.cjs`, `server.js`, `js/`, `styles/`, `images/`, the `.ps1` scripts, `src/pages/`) is legacy, superseded by `web/`. Do not fix bugs in it or extend it — it exists only until the removal phases below are done.
- Render (the old `server.js` API) has been suspended since 2026-09-22 and confirmed unused by the live site. Don't add new references to it or to its onrender.com URL.

## DATABASE — SACRED
Tables: `colors`, `print_jobs`, `shops`, `site_traffic`. No schema changes, renamed or dropped columns, or new tables without explicit approval in the current session. Never run raw DDL. Every UPDATE/DELETE needs a row-level filter (`.eq(...)` or equivalent) — never an unfiltered bulk write.

## SECRETS
- No hardcoded keys, tokens, or passwords in source, ever, including as a fallback ORed against an env var in an auth check. (A hardcoded admin-key bypass was found in `server.js` during the audit — don't reintroduce that pattern anywhere.)
- Client-exposed values are limited to `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars (the Supabase anon key is safe here — RLS is the real security layer). Admin keys and webhook URLs are server-only, read via `process.env` inside Route Handlers, never sent to the browser.

## DEPLOYMENT
- Never run `vercel --prod` or `vercel deploy --prod` manually. Production deploys happen only through `git push origin main` via Vercel's Git integration.
- PowerShell only, not CMD.
- Don't leave `npm run dev` or other long-running processes running after a task finishes — close the terminal pane.

## PROJECT LOG
Keep `Project_Log.md` entries short: what changed, which files, one line on how it was verified. Don't re-read the whole file each task — the entry at the top is enough context to continue. Flag it once it passes ~300 lines so old entries can be archived instead of endlessly reread.

## CLEANUP ROADMAP — ONE PHASE AT A TIME, ONE COMMIT PER PHASE
Don't start a phase until the previous one is committed and confirmed working on the live site. Don't combine phases into one commit.

1. ✅ Done (2026-09-23, commit `f05ab27`). Removed `api/env.js` — dead, confirmed 404, superseded by Next.js env handling.
2. ✅ Done (2026-09-23, commit `5f8ed19`). Removed the retired Electron desktop app: `main.cjs`, root `hub.html`, `src/pages/`, root `icon.png` / `icon-maskable.png`, `dist/`, `dist_build.log`, and the build scripts (`final_build.ps1`, `check_and_build.ps1`, `kill_and_build.ps1`, `find_lock*.ps1`, `force_clean_build.ps1`, `run_dist.ps1`, `verify_hub.ps1`).
3. ✅ Done (2026-09-23, commit `57315c2`). Removed the legacy root static site: `index.html`, `gallery.html`, `contact.html`, `meettheteam.html`, `request.html`, `inventory.html`, `styles/`, `js/`, root `images/`, `gallery/`, `manifest.json`, `Crafted 3D.ico`, `check_lock.ps1`, `output.txt`, `test_ignore_file.txt`. (Note: `gallery/` and `js/` remain on disk as empty folders — git doesn't track empty dirs — harmless, delete manually whenever.)
4. ✅ Done (2026-09-23, commit `b28b18e`). Removed `server.js`, root `package-lock.json`, and untracked root `node_modules/`. Reduced root `package.json` to metadata-only (`name`, `version`, `description`, `private`, `repository`, `license`) with a retirement notice. Root `.env` is now fully unused (was only read by `server.js`) but was deliberately left in place — delete manually whenever ready.
5. Delete the `feature/universal-web-target` branch, local and remote.
6. Rewrite root `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` so they describe `web/` as the live app. Remove references to `mobile-companion`, the Express/Render backend, and the old sandbox-branch policy.
